__pycache__/
.claude/settings.local.json
# Nested worktree checkouts the Claude Code harness creates here -- each is a
# full copy of the repo. Without this the link check would recurse into them:
# `hidden = true` in `lychee.toml` puts every dotdir in its walk.
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
.env
.venv/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ty_cache/
.rumdl_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
# Per-member `coverage json` report, written by `pytest` (`--cov-report=json`
# in each member's `addopts`) for `scripts/coverage_floor.py` to read. Anchored
# to the member dirs, not `coverage.json` anywhere, so a same-named test
# fixture nested deeper (e.g. under `tests/fixtures/`) stays trackable.
/packages/*/coverage.json
# The same report at the root, which a `pytest` started from the repo root
# writes instead. Nothing reads it — the floor check is per member — and it has
# been committed by accident more than once.
/coverage.json
# mise resolves external QA tools at `latest`; the lockfile is not pinned, so a
# locally-generated one is never committed.
mise.lock
